1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,924
Zoya and her Nani made fifty laddoos.

2
00:00:03,224 --> 00:00:04,568
They tasted great.

3
00:00:04,568 --> 00:00:06,386
But Zoya sold only eight.

4
00:00:06,936 --> 00:00:08,125
What went wrong?

5
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:10,454
Zoya never asked what people wanted.

6
00:00:11,104 --> 00:00:12,408
Meet Laddoo Lab.

7
00:00:12,408 --> 00:00:17,145
Zoya, a college student in Bengaluru,
wants to turn Nani's laddoos into

8
00:00:17,145 --> 00:00:18,045
a brand.

9
00:00:18,311 --> 00:00:22,982
The recipe uses ragi, a healthy millet,
and jaggery, a natural sweetener

10
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:24,103
from sugarcane.

11
00:00:24,453 --> 00:00:26,594
Her brother Arjun handles sales.

12
00:00:26,594 --> 00:00:28,745
Her friend Dev does the design.

13
00:00:29,395 --> 00:00:30,920
So what is marketing?

14
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:36,067
Philip Kotler and Gary Armstrong wrote
the textbook, Principles of Marketing.

15
00:00:36,417 --> 00:00:41,311
They say marketing creates value for
customers and builds strong relationships,

16
00:00:41,311 --> 00:00:43,265
to capture value in return.

17
00:00:43,615 --> 00:00:46,301
Value means the good you
get for what you pay.

18
00:00:46,651 --> 00:00:50,533
In simple words: find what people
need, serve them better than others,

19
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:52,104
and keep them coming back.

20
00:00:52,754 --> 00:00:54,178
First, the selling way.

21
00:00:54,528 --> 00:00:58,056
Zoya makes fifty big laddoos,
and waits at the college gate.

22
00:00:58,406 --> 00:00:59,888
People walk past.

23
00:00:59,888 --> 00:01:01,023
A few stop.

24
00:01:01,023 --> 00:01:02,030
Most don't.

25
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:04,742
Eight sold, forty two left over.

26
00:01:04,742 --> 00:01:06,889
Wasted money and wasted effort.

27
00:01:07,539 --> 00:01:08,977
Now the marketing way.

28
00:01:08,977 --> 00:01:11,763
First, Zoya asks the
parents in her building.

29
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:15,260
They want a healthy sweet
for school tiffin boxes.

30
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:17,518
Small, and with no refined sugar.

31
00:01:17,868 --> 00:01:21,810
So Nani makes small laddoos, and
Arjun takes them door to door.

32
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,893
This time, forty six of fifty are sold.

33
00:01:24,893 --> 00:01:27,262
Same kitchen, a far better result.

34
00:01:27,912 --> 00:01:29,712
Selling pushes what you made.

35
00:01:29,712 --> 00:01:31,691
Marketing makes what people need.

36
00:01:32,391 --> 00:01:34,181
Peter Drucker put it best.

37
00:01:34,181 --> 00:01:38,622
The aim of marketing is to know and
understand the customer so well, the

38
00:01:38,622 --> 00:01:41,505
product or service fits
him and sells itself.

39
00:01:42,155 --> 00:01:44,215
Marketing works through exchange.

40
00:01:44,215 --> 00:01:46,690
Both sides give, and both sides get.

41
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,641
Laddoo Lab gives Mrs.

42
00:01:48,641 --> 00:01:52,167
Rao a healthy snack, and
time saved every morning.

43
00:01:52,517 --> 00:01:53,417
Mrs.

44
00:01:53,035 --> 00:01:57,005
Rao gives back money, a hundred
and twenty rupees for six.

45
00:01:57,355 --> 00:01:58,463
Both sides win.

46
00:01:58,463 --> 00:02:01,796
And because she is happy,
she comes back every week.

47
00:02:01,796 --> 00:02:03,336
That is a relationship.

48
00:02:03,986 --> 00:02:07,238
Kotler and Armstrong show
marketing as five steps.

49
00:02:07,588 --> 00:02:08,488
One.

50
00:02:08,148 --> 00:02:10,390
Understand what customers need.

51
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:11,590
Two.

52
00:02:11,155 --> 00:02:13,929
Choose whom to serve,
and how to stand out.

53
00:02:14,229 --> 00:02:15,129
Three.

54
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:18,064
Make the right product,
price, place and promotion.

55
00:02:18,364 --> 00:02:19,264
Four.

56
00:02:18,979 --> 00:02:21,163
Build relationships that last.

57
00:02:21,464 --> 00:02:22,364
Five.

58
00:02:22,062 --> 00:02:26,167
Capture value back, as sales,
profit and loyal customers.

59
00:02:26,817 --> 00:02:28,784
Where do we see this at work today?

60
00:02:29,134 --> 00:02:30,034
Needs.

61
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:31,339
Ask before you make.

62
00:02:31,339 --> 00:02:34,311
A phone maker asks users what annoys them.

63
00:02:34,661 --> 00:02:35,561
Value.

64
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:36,898
More good for the price.

65
00:02:36,898 --> 00:02:40,120
A bank opens your account
on your phone in minutes.

66
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:41,370
Exchange.

67
00:02:41,302 --> 00:02:42,593
Both sides win.

68
00:02:42,593 --> 00:02:45,811
A bakery sells fresh
bread at a fair price.

69
00:02:46,161 --> 00:02:47,211
Relationships.

70
00:02:47,211 --> 00:02:48,593
Bring people back.

71
00:02:48,593 --> 00:02:52,002
A food delivery app remembers
your favourite order.

72
00:02:52,652 --> 00:02:54,514
But is marketing always good?

73
00:02:54,514 --> 00:02:56,291
It depends how you use it.

74
00:02:56,641 --> 00:02:57,730
The good side.

75
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:00,995
People find what they need,
and small makers grow.

76
00:03:01,345 --> 00:03:02,469
The hard side.

77
00:03:02,469 --> 00:03:05,641
Some ads lie, or push
things people don't need.

78
00:03:05,991 --> 00:03:08,840
Dev wants to print sugar free on the pack.

79
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,905
Nani says no.

80
00:03:09,905 --> 00:03:11,522
Jaggery is still sugar.

81
00:03:11,872 --> 00:03:14,286
So the pack says, no refined sugar.

82
00:03:14,286 --> 00:03:16,049
True, and still tempting.

83
00:03:16,399 --> 00:03:22,142
In India, the Consumer Protection Act
of 2019 allows fines up to ten lakh

84
00:03:22,142 --> 00:03:24,358
rupees for misleading ads.

85
00:03:24,708 --> 00:03:25,649
The lesson?

86
00:03:25,649 --> 00:03:28,269
Win customers with truth, not tricks.

87
00:03:28,919 --> 00:03:29,851
Quick check.

88
00:03:29,851 --> 00:03:33,501
Zoya asks parents what they
need before she makes anything.

89
00:03:33,501 --> 00:03:34,837
What is she doing?

90
00:03:36,737 --> 00:03:37,637
Marketing!

91
00:03:37,466 --> 00:03:40,888
She starts with the customer's
need, not with the product.

92
00:03:41,488 --> 00:03:42,501
So, remember.

93
00:03:42,801 --> 00:03:46,697
Marketing means finding what people
need, and serving them better than

94
00:03:46,697 --> 00:03:47,597
others.

95
00:03:47,643 --> 00:03:51,600
It works through exchange: value
goes one way, money comes back.

96
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:54,991
And it builds relationships,
so customers come back.

97
00:03:55,591 --> 00:03:59,484
Next time, we'll explore marketing
concepts and orientations.
